EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       mmoovvee__mmoouunntt() can be used to move attached mounts like the following:

           move_mount(AT_FDCWD, "/a", AT_FDCWD, "/b", 0);

       This would move the mount object mounted on _/_a to _/_b.  The above proce‐
       dure  is functionally equivalent to the following mount operation using
       mmoouunntt(2):

           mount("/a", "/b", NULL, MS_MOVE, NULL);

       mmoovvee__mmoouunntt() can also be used in conjunction with file descriptors  re‐
       turned from ooppeenn__ttrreeee(2) or ooppeenn(2):

           int fd = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, "/mnt", 0); /* open("/mnt", O_PATH); */
           move_mount(fd, "", AT_FDCWD, "/mnt2", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);
           move_mount(fd, "", AT_FDCWD, "/mnt3", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);
           move_mount(fd, "", AT_FDCWD, "/mnt4", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);

       This  would move the mount object mounted at _/_m_n_t to _/_m_n_t_2, then _/_m_n_t_3,
       and then _/_m_n_t_4.

       If the source mount object indicated by _f_r_o_m___d_i_r_f_d and _f_r_o_m___p_a_t_h  is  a
       detached mount object, mmoovvee__mmoouunntt() can be used to attach it to a mount
       point:

           int fsfd, mntfd;

           fsfd = fsopen("ext4", FSOPEN_CLOEXEC);
           fsconfig(fsfd, FSCONFIG_SET_STRING, "source", "/dev/sda1", 0);
           fsconfig(fsfd, FSCONFIG_SET_FLAG, "user_xattr", NULL, 0);
           fsconfig(fsfd, FSCONFIG_CMD_CREATE, NULL, NULL, 0);
           mntfd = fsmount(fsfd, FSMOUNT_CLOEXEC, MOUNT_ATTR_NODEV);
           move_mount(mntfd, "", AT_FDCWD, "/home", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);

       This would create a new filesystem configuration context for ext4, con‐
       figure it, create a detached mount object, and then attach it to _/_h_o_m_e.
       The  above  procedure is functionally equivalent to the following mount
       operation using mmoouunntt(2):

           mount("/dev/sda1", "/home", "ext4", MS_NODEV, "user_xattr");

       The same operation also works with detached  bind‐mounts  created  with
       ooppeenn__ttrreeee(2) with OOPPEENN__TTRREEEE__CCLLOONNEE:

           int mntfd = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, "/home/cyphar", OPEN_TREE_CLONE);
           move_mount(mntfd, "", AT_FDCWD, "/root", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);

